endently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-098529","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-10","reportDate":"2026-09-09","cik":"0001966750","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966750/000121390026098529/ea030476301ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c76875556f69c0e25f9f9f733f27c478cf6d57991f52b516fe0178448360805e.bin","sha256":"c76875556f69c0e25f9f9f733f27c478cf6d57991f52b516fe0178448360805e"}}],"omittedEvidenceCount":0},"managementExplanations":{"status":"no_evidence","evidence":[],"omittedEvidenceCount":0},"materialEvents":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"872bd8795fc8228ea9a33cf0f55ec53d8a0f7462216ac1f90a2262799e680346","quote":"Only shareholders of the Company of record at the close of business on September 1, 2026 (the “Record Date”) are entitled to attend and vote at the Meeting or at any adjournment thereof. Quorum, for purposes of the Meeting, consists of at least one or more shareholders present or by proxy, or if a corporation, by its duly authorized representative, representing not less than one-third of the issued and outstanding Class A ordinary shares and Class B ordinary shares which are entitled to vote at such general meeting of the Company. As of the Record Date, there were 449,264,625 Class A ordinary shares and there were no Class B ordinary shares issued and outstanding, with each Class A ordinary shares entitled to one vote per share and each Class B ordinary shares entitled to 20 votes per share.","context":"RECORD DATE; VOTING POWER","section":"","block":49,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-098529","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-10","reportDate":"2026-09-09","cik":"0001966750","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966750/000121390026098529/ea030476301ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c76875556f69c0e25f9f9f733f27c478cf6d57991f52b516fe0178448360805e.bin","sha256":"c76875556f69c0e25f9f9f733f27c478cf6d57991f52b516fe0178448360805e"}},{"id":"7297779e9251bd67adc98d6061192e0b80f481f08d08f5ef4460c488c3a14a1a","quote":"Proposal No. 3 — The Share Consolidation Proposal: to approve, by ordinary resolution, subject to the Share Capital Increase Proposal being passed at the Meeting and the closing bid price on any trading day of the Company's Class A ordinary shares with a par value of US$0.0001 each listed on Nasdaq Capital Market being below US$0.12 per share (“Trigger Event”), a consolidation of the Company’s authorised, issued and outstanding Class A ordinary shares and Class B ordinary shares of the Company (collectively, the “Shares”), by consolidating each 50 Shares of the Company into 1 Share of the Company, with such consolidated Shares having the same rights and being subject to the same restrictions (save as to nominal value) as the existing Shares of such class as set out in the A&R M&A (the “Share Consolidation”), such Share Consolidation taking effect on the 15th trading day after the Trigger Event or such later date as accepted by NASDAQ.","context":"Proposal No. 2 — The Memorandum and Articles Amendment No. 1 Proposal: by special resolution, subject to Proposal 1 above being passed at the Meeting and upon effectiveness of the Share Capital Increase, to adopt an amended and restated memorandum and articles of association to reflect, inter alia, the Share Capital Increase, the provision of veto rights over decisions of the Board to Botao Ma, and amendments to permit a director to vote, and be counted in the quorum, on any matter in which he or she is interested subject to disclosure of that interest (the “A&R M&A”).","section":"","block":54,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-098529","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-10","reportDate":"2026-09-09","cik":"0001966750","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966750/000121390026098529/ea030476301ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c76875556f69c0e25f9f9f733f27c478cf6d57991f52b516fe0178448360805e.bin","sha256":"c76875556f69c0e25f9f9f733f27c478cf6d57991f52b516fe0178448360805e"}},{"id":"bf29b805323bca8896e3cf162a02143723bb1b2f4f291d3f913408c3d7749363","quote":"Our Board has determined, subject to the Share Capital Increase Proposal being approved at the Meeting and following the Share Capital Increase being effected, it is advisable and in the best interests of the Company and its shareholders, for the Company to adopt an amended and restated memorandum and articles of association of the Company to reflect, among other things: (i) the Share Capital Increase; (ii) that any questions which arise in a meeting of the directors must be decided by a majority of votes of the directors present and voting, provided always that, where Mr. Botao Ma (or his duly appointed designee) is present at the meeting, such majority must include the affirmative vote of Mr. Ma (or, where applicable, his duly appointed alternate) (the “Veto Right”), however, if Mr. Ma had received the notice of such meeting and is absent or if Mr. Ma is not entitled to vote pursuant to Article 19 of the amended and restated memorandum and articles of association, then the Board may determine any questions without the vote or consent of Mr. Ma, and (iii) to amend the provisions on permissible directors’ interests so that a director may vote, and be counted in the quorum, on any matter in which he or she is interested, subject to disclosure of that interest, in the form attached hereto as Annex A.","context":"GENERAL","section":"","block":89,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-098529","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-10","reportDate":"2026-09-09","cik":"0001966750","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966750/000121390026098529/ea030476301ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c76875556f69c0e25f9f9f733f27c4